---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Germany, not Scandinavia should be the HDI benchmark"
  description="Comparing HDIs of G20 nations"
>
  <article class="visual-essay">
    <header class="essay-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Visual essay</p>
      <h1>Germany, not Scandinavia should be the HDI benchmark</h1>
      <p class="dek">Comparing HDIs of G20 nations</p>
    </header>

    <p>
      The trigger for this article - I was traveling through Germany, and I realised that its trains, offices and public services were much better compared to the UK. This is reflected in Deutschland's stellar HDI. Normally you think of Scandinavia as the standard, but probably Germany should be. Besides US, it's the only large country that has pulled this off. 
    </p> 
    <p>
      For this analysis, I have excluded India and China to avoid using a log scale x axis. Their average HDI (Human Development Index) scores over
      2019–23 were <strong>0.662</strong> and <strong>0.791</strong>. 
    </p>

    <section class="chart-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="figure-number">01</p>
        <h2>HDI among large countries</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-scroll">
        <svg id="hdi-full" viewBox="0 0 930 570" role="img" aria-label="Population and average HDI among G20 countries below 400 million people"></svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p>
      As you can see, among G20 countries with fewer than 400 million people, Germany stands out. It sustains an
      average HDI of <strong>0.957</strong> across a population of more than 80 million. That too, despite high levels of immigration. In 2023,
      15% of its residents were foreign nationals. It's the only country that comes very close to Scandinavia and has sustained a high HDI for the last 20 years.
    </p>

    <p>
      As we all know, Scandinavia is the benchmark for HDI - averaging <strong>0.961</strong> across Denmark, Norway
      and Sweden. But the average Scandinavian country has only 7.3 million people. It becomes difficult to sustain a high HDI at higher population levels.
    </p>

    <section class="chart-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="figure-number">02</p>
        <h2>The high-HDI group</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-scroll">
        <svg id="hdi-zoom" viewBox="0 0 930 570" role="img" aria-label="Magnified comparison of countries with a higher average HDI than Türkiye"></svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p>
      The United States is the other exception. No country in this comparison combines a population
      above 300 million with an HDI above 0.9. Its score of <strong>0.930</strong> trails Germany,
      but achieving it across 343 million people still makes the US an outlier.
    </p>

    <section class="chart-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="figure-number">03</p>
        <h2>A closer look below 150 million</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-scroll">
        <svg id="hdi-close" viewBox="0 0 930 570" role="img" aria-label="Close comparison of high-HDI countries below 150 million people, with the United States retained as an off-scale reference"></svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="chart-key" aria-label="Chart key">
      <span><i class="peer"></i>G20 peer</span><span><i class="germany"></i>Germany</span>
      <span><i class="usa"></i>United States</span><span><i class="scandinavia"></i>Scandinavia average</span>
    </div>

    <footer class="sources">
      <p><strong>Method.</strong> HDI is the simple average for 2019–23; population is for 2023. Scandinavia is the unweighted average of Denmark, Norway and Sweden. Figure 03 excludes Türkiye and countries below it, then magnifies countries below 150 million; the US remains as an off-scale reference.</p>
      <p><strong>Sources.</strong> <a href="https://hdr.undp.org/data-center/documentation-and-downloads">UNDP Human Development Report data</a>; <a href="https://www.destatis.de/EN/Themes/Society-Environment/Population/Current-Population/Tables/population-by-laender.html">German Federal Statistical Office</a>.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
(() => {
  const data = [
    ['AR','Argentina',45.538,.8564],['AU','Australia',26.451,.9522],['BR','Brazil',211.141,.7760],
    ['CA','Canada',39.299,.9358],['FR','France',66.439,.9148],['DE','Germany',84.548,.9568],
    ['ID','Indonesia',281.190,.7170],['IT','Italy',59.499,.9066],['JP','Japan',124.371,.9224],
    ['MX','Mexico',129.740,.7768],['KR','South Korea',51.749,.9306],['RU','Russia',145.441,.8272],
    ['SA','Saudi Arabia',33.264,.8848],['ZA','South Africa',63.212,.7330],['TR','Türkiye',87.271,.8452],
    ['UK','United Kingdom',68.683,.9408],['US','United States',343.477,.9300],
    ['SC','Scandinavia average',7.339,.9607]
  ].map(([code,name,pop,hdi]) => ({code,name,pop,hdi}));
  const ns = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const make = (tag, attrs = {}, text = '') => {
    const element = document.createElementNS(ns, tag);
    Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([key,value]) => element.setAttribute(key, String(value)));
    if (text) element.textContent = text;
    return element;
  };
  const draw = ({id,minHdi,maxPop,filter,offScaleUS = false}) => {
    const svg = document.querySelector(id);
    if (!svg) return;
    const plot = {left:90,right:890,top:54,bottom:500};
    const x = pop => plot.left + (pop / maxPop) * (plot.right - plot.left);
    const y = hdi => plot.top + ((1 - hdi) / (1 - minHdi)) * (plot.bottom - plot.top);
    const rows = data.filter(filter);
    const step = minHdi >= .84 ? .02 : .05;
    const ticks = [];
    for (let value = 1; value >= minHdi - .0001; value -= step) ticks.push(Number(value.toFixed(2)));
    svg.append(make('desc',{},'Country codes are printed inside each point; population increases rightward and HDI shortfall increases downward.'));
    ticks.forEach(tick => {
      const py = y(tick);
      svg.append(make('line',{class:'gridline',x1:plot.left,y1:py,x2:plot.right,y2:py}));
      svg.append(make('text',{class:'tick',x:plot.left-16,y:py+4,'text-anchor':'end'},tick === 1 ? '0' : `−${(1-tick).toFixed(2).replace('0.','.')}`));
    });
    const xStep = maxPop > 300 ? 100 : 50;
    for (let tick = 0; tick <= maxPop; tick += xStep) {
      svg.append(make('text',{class:'tick',x:x(tick),y:532,'text-anchor':'middle'},tick === 0 ? '0' : `${tick}m`));
    }
    svg.append(make('line',{class:'axis',x1:plot.left,y1:plot.top,x2:plot.right,y2:plot.top}));
    svg.append(make('line',{class:'axis',x1:plot.left,y1:plot.top,x2:plot.left,y2:plot.bottom}));
    svg.append(make('path',{class:'arrow',d:`M${plot.right} ${plot.top}l-10-5v10z`}));
    svg.append(make('path',{class:'arrow',d:`M${plot.left} ${plot.bottom}l-5-10h10z`}));
    svg.append(make('text',{class:'axis-label',x:490,y:562,'text-anchor':'middle'},'Population in 2023 · linear scale'));
    svg.append(make('text',{class:'axis-label',x:23,y:277,'text-anchor':'middle',transform:'rotate(-90 23 277)'},'Average HDI distance from 1.0 · 2019–23'));
    rows.forEach(d => {
      const group = make('g',{class:`mark mark-${d.code.toLowerCase()}`});
      group.append(make('title',{},`${d.name}: ${d.pop.toFixed(1)}m people; ${d.hdi.toFixed(3)} average HDI`));
      group.append(make('circle',{cx:x(d.pop),cy:y(d.hdi),r:13}));
      group.append(make('text',{x:x(d.pop),y:y(d.hdi)+4,'text-anchor':'middle'},d.code));
      svg.append(group);
    });
    if (offScaleUS) {
      const py = y(.9300);
      svg.append(make('line',{class:'us-reference',x1:plot.right-92,y1:py,x2:plot.right,y2:py}));
      svg.append(make('path',{class:'us-arrow',d:`M${plot.right} ${py}l-10-5v10z`}));
      svg.append(make('text',{class:'us-label',x:plot.right-98,y:py+4,'text-anchor':'end'},'US · 343m · .930'));
    }
  };
  draw({id:'#hdi-full',minHdi:.65,maxPop:350,filter:() => true});
  draw({id:'#hdi-zoom',minHdi:.84,maxPop:350,filter:d => d.hdi > .8452});
  draw({id:'#hdi-close',minHdi:.84,maxPop:150,filter:d => d.hdi > .8452 && d.pop < 150 && d.code !== 'US',offScaleUS:true});
})();
</script>

<style>
  .visual-essay { --cobalt:#3D5FA8; --teal:#28766F; --mustard:#C7922F; --vermilion:#D05A3A; }
  .essay-header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .eyebrow, .figure-number { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .8rem; color: var(--color-accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .essay-header h1 { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .dek { max-width: 620px; color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .visual-essay > p { max-width: 680px; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .chart-section { margin: 3rem 0; }
  .section-heading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .8rem; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .section-heading h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .figure-number { margin: 0; }
  .chart-scroll { overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: visible; scrollbar-width: thin; }
  .chart-scroll svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; overflow: visible; }
  :global(.gridline) { stroke: #E6E3DC; stroke-width: 1; }
  :global(.axis) { stroke: #5F6265; stroke-width: 1.2; }
  :global(.arrow) { fill: #5F6265; }
  :global(.tick) { fill: #5F6265; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; }
  :global(.axis-label) { fill: #181A1B; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 14px; }
  :global(.mark circle) { fill: var(--cobalt); stroke: var(--color-bg); stroke-width: 2; }
  :global(.mark text) { fill: #FCFBF8; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 500; pointer-events: none; }
  :global(.mark-de circle) { fill: var(--mustard); }
  :global(.mark-us circle) { fill: var(--vermilion); }
  :global(.mark-sc circle) { fill: var(--teal); }
  :global(.us-reference) { stroke: var(--vermilion); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  :global(.us-arrow) { fill: var(--vermilion); }
  :global(.us-label) { fill: #181A1B; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 500; }
  .chart-key { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .7rem 1.2rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; font-size: .85rem; }
  .chart-key span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .chart-key i { width: .65rem; height: .65rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--cobalt); }
  .chart-key .germany { background: var(--mustard); }
  .chart-key .usa { background: var(--vermilion); }
  .chart-key .scandinavia { background: var(--teal); }
  .sources { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .sources p { margin-bottom: .65rem; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .section-heading { align-items: flex-start; } .visual-essay > p { font-size: 1rem; } }
</style>
